WEBVTT

00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.100
Your business made a profit.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:04.267
So why can’t you pay the bills?

00:00:04.757 --> 00:00:08.791
Imagine a small business
delivers a $10,000 order.

00:00:08.791 --> 00:00:10.908
The products cost $7,000.

00:00:10.908 --> 00:00:13.018
That’s $3,000 of profit,

00:00:13.018 --> 00:00:15.530
before tax and other expenses.

00:00:16.270 --> 00:00:18.737
But the customer
can pay in 60 days.

00:00:18.737 --> 00:00:21.024
Your supplier needs
paying in 15.

00:00:21.024 --> 00:00:23.397
And you only have
$4,000 in the bank.

00:00:24.437 --> 00:00:26.105
Day 15 arrives.

00:00:26.295 --> 00:00:27.971
$7,000 is due.

00:00:27.971 --> 00:00:29.228
You have four.

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:30.728
You’re $3,000 short,

00:00:30.728 --> 00:00:32.936
even though the sale
was profitable.

00:00:33.876 --> 00:00:36.279
An invoice is
a request for payment.

00:00:36.279 --> 00:00:38.032
It isn’t money in your bank.

00:00:38.032 --> 00:00:40.892
Cash flow is money
actually moving in and out.

00:00:41.182 --> 00:00:43.563
And the customer
isn’t even late yet.

00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:45.406
These are the terms
you agreed.

00:00:46.096 --> 00:00:49.136
In a 2026 Intuit
QuickBooks report,

00:00:49.136 --> 00:00:51.489
39% of surveyed
US business owners

00:00:51.489 --> 00:00:56.667
said one late payment made it
hard to cover payroll or bills.

00:00:57.657 --> 00:00:59.867
More orders can make
the gap bigger

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:02.868
if you must pay for them
before customers pay you.

00:01:03.558 --> 00:01:06.438
Before taking an order,
map the payment dates.

00:01:06.438 --> 00:01:09.690
Where possible, agree
a deposit or better timing.

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.203
And keep a cash cushion.

00:01:14.793 --> 00:01:17.433
As an investor,
ask three questions.

00:01:17.433 --> 00:01:19.206
When does the money arrive?

00:01:19.206 --> 00:01:20.741
What is due first?

00:01:20.741 --> 00:01:22.211
What covers the gap?

00:01:22.801 --> 00:01:24.675
Profit tells you what you earned.

00:01:24.675 --> 00:01:26.878
Cash tells you
what you can pay today.
